    <layouts>
      <layout name="RootLayout" file="src/layouts/root.tsx">
        <description>Wraps the app. Subscribes to service.config.size.changes and, in a layout effect, toggles the `small` class on &lt;body&gt; before paint, which is what drives every Tailwind `small:` variant.</description>
      </layout>
      <layout name="AuthLayout" file="src/layouts/authenticated/index.tsx">
        <description>Subscribes to service.auth.changes; a null session redirects to /login. Renders the sticky Topbar (bg-sky-300, h-16 / small:h-12), the main-body div, the Outlet, and the sonner Toaster. Registers the alt+N navigation shortcuts.</description>
        <note>The shell is the height chain's root: it is `h-dvh` (a definite height, matching body and #root) and `#main-body` is `flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto`. With `min-h-screen` the shell's height was content-based, so every `h-full` page only resolved while it happened to fit; a long record silently grew past the viewport, and `body { overflow-y-hidden }` clipped it with no scrollbar anywhere. Pages that need a scrollport now get a definite height from this chain — do not go back to auto/min-height on the shell.</note>
        <component name="Topbar" file="z-Topbar.tsx">
          <description>Sticky header. Left: a back button unless on "/", the route title (longest-prefix match over a title map) and a dynamic Title. Right: TopNavList and the settings/reload actions. Titles: Beranda, Toko, Metode, Pelanggan, Kasir, Kontak, Produk, Biaya Lainnya, Riwayat, Analisis, Uang, Pengaturan — several of which name routes that are currently disabled.</description>
